preConditionHook:
// EL: upperTailBars = CountIF(high - MaxList(open, close)
//         >= tailFraction * (high - low), windowBars),
// and the mirror on the lower tail for the short side.
//
// The LONG side counts UPPER tails, which is the BEARISH reading -- the same
// orientation GrowingTopTails carries -- so a with-trend long filter negates
// the placement.
//
// CountIF counts bars 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar and its argument is a
// true SERIES (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED): every price term shifts with
// the counted bar, which is what this loop does. The counted terms are prices
// with real history, so no zero-filled variable mirror is needed.
//
// MaxList / MinList select among open and close -- tick-grid PRICE operands,
// the scope their ACCEPTED row allows -- so plain > / < stand in, exactly as
// AverageUpperTailFraction writes the same selection.
//
// Products, not quotients: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero error
// on a zero denominator and a zero-range bar is legal data.
// The counts and the selections are class members and persist across bars, so
// they are reset or reassigned before use.
upperTailBars = 0.0;
lowerTailBars = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)windowBars; ++i) {
    bodyTop = open[i];
    if (close[i] > bodyTop) bodyTop = close[i];
    bodyBottom = open[i];
    if (close[i] < bodyBottom) bodyBottom = close[i];
    if (el_ge(high[i] - bodyTop, tailFraction * (high[i] - low[i]))) {
        upperTailBars = upperTailBars + 1;
    }
    if (el_ge(bodyBottom - low[i], tailFraction * (high[i] - low[i]))) {
        lowerTailBars = lowerTailBars + 1;
    }
}
